#: ../../source/tutorials-md/05-troubleshooting/README.md:618
#: 0e751fe897b94c45a98e3f18215d91a9
msgid "Tips for Successful Troubleshooting"
msgstr "نکتهs برای Successful عیب‌یابی"

#: ../../source/tutorials-md/05-troubleshooting/README.md:620
#: 7a9004be07c640ffbf0c10a1c71e32d6
msgid ""
"✅ **Read error messages carefully**: They usually tell you exactly what's"
" wrong ✅ **Start simple**: Test with minimal system first (2-4 atoms) ✅ "
"**One change at a time**: Don't modify 5 parameters simultaneously ✅ "
"**Compare with working case**: If Si works but your system doesn't, "
"what's different? ✅ **Check literature**: Has anyone calculated this "
"material before? ✅ **Use custodian**: Let it fix common errors "
"automatically ✅ **Document what works**: Save working parameter sets for "
"similar systems ✅ **Don't over-tighten**: Tighter ≠ better (diminishing "
"returns after convergence)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials-md/05-troubleshooting/README.md:631
#: 3098d2ae9e074f37bbd82c647261a132
msgid "Common Misconceptions"
msgstr "Common Misconceptions"

#: ../../source/tutorials-md/05-troubleshooting/README.md:633
#: fc54d1ef48674754917ae3375f1a576c
msgid ""
"❌ **\"More k-points is always better\"**    → After convergence (~0.01 "
"eV), more k-points just waste time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials-md/05-troubleshooting/README.md:636
#: 845cb437544b4952b0d69a86b9a6eae6
msgid ""
"❌ **\"SCF must converge to 1e-8\"**    → 1e-4 is usually sufficient; 1e-5"
" for forces; 1e-6 for phonons"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials-md/05-troubleshooting/README.md:639
#: f3e5296bc60840a1a341887c413389ca
#, python-format
msgid ""
"❌ **\"Calculation failed → SIESTA bug\"**    → 99% of failures are "
"parameter/input issues, not code bugs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials-md/05-troubleshooting/README.md:642
#: fee5ca7c95e94aed9771490779a05947
msgid ""
"❌ **\"DZP always better than DZ\"**    → For band gaps, maybe. For total "
"energies, sometimes worse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials-md/05-troubleshooting/README.md:645
#: 6e4c27f4bb5f47bc813acf0498223757
msgid ""
"❌ **\"Hybrid functionals fix all problems\"**    → They fix band gaps, "
"not SCF convergence. Use GGA first."
msgstr ""

